# Job: go binding — R3 review defects (F-R3-1, F-R3-12, F-R3-17)

You are a codex sub-agent under a Claude supervisor. Model gpt-6-astra, reasoning xhigh. Cap 3 h. Read `AGENTS.md` (root) §2/§3/§4.1/§5, `bindings/AGENTS.md` (if present) and the language AGENTS.md. Campaign rules (`doc/plan/c016-worklog/decisions.ko.md` D-098, D-109, D-111): one owner per rule, fewer rules, no mitigations (no timeouts/retries/second pollers/catch-alls), cross-language parity mandatory, regression test per fix, public API unchanged unless the cause says otherwise. Never modify `core/**`, any `doc/spec/**`, `framework/**`, `doc/site/**`, other bindings. Never lower an assertion. Do not commit — one separable diff per cause, describe the split (files/hunks) in the summary. Owner contracts: `core/doc/spec/core/socket/README.ko.md` (§ part send / REQUEST DONTWAIT / completion pull and ownership / §6 completion table), `bindings/doc/spec/async-execution-model.ko.md`, `bindings/doc/spec/async-coroutine-policy.ko.md`. Diagnosis source (verified by the supervisor, D-109/D-111): `doc/plan/c016-worklog/spec-review/R3-bindings-summary.md`. Reference implementations that already satisfy a rule are named per cause. Gate: the binding's `tests/run_tests.sh` (0 failures; use `ZLINK_CORE_SOURCE=local` where the script supports it, Core lib `core/build-dev`) plus the new tests 5x, and the binding samples via the same script if it runs them (take `/tmp/zlink-samples-gate.lock` with flock while samples run). Do not run perf benchmarks.

## Causes
1. **F-R3-1 — WRITABLE peer RID re-verification.** The binding finds the waiter by socket-local context/token and then compares `completion.peer_rid` with the original target, turning a mismatch into `INTERNAL_ERROR`/EPROTO. Core guarantees the submit RID echo (socket README part send: "`peer_rid`는 ROUTER·STREAM에서 submit RID, PAIR·DEALER에서 empty"); the binding must deliver the WRITABLE found by context/token to that waiter without re-judging the RID (bindings README, D-109 sentence). Remove the comparison and the allocations made only for it (e.g. building a `RoutingId`, `ToBytes()`); keep the kind/context checks. Behavior is unchanged for a conforming Core; add a test that a WRITABLE for the waiter's token is delivered to it.  Code: `bindings/go/internal/native/completion_owner.go:683-689`, `:781-804`, `dealer_router_request.go:126-134`.
2. **F-R3-12 — resubmit before NO_DATA.** The drain loop resubmits the retained record inline while capturing the WRITABLE, so the retry's new completion can be consumed by the same drain. Core rule (socket README part send / REQUEST DONTWAIT): the caller drains the completion queue to `NO_DATA` and only then resubmits. Reference: dotnet `bindings/dotnet/src/Zlink/Runtime/Messaging/CompletionOwner.cs:349-400` (`_retries` list, retried after `NO_DATA`; D-B117). Collect retries during the drain and run them after `NO_DATA`; no extra poller/timer. Test: a WRITABLE captured mid-drain is resubmitted only after the drain reached NO_DATA (observable through the order of a second queued completion vs the resubmit).  Code: `completion_owner.go:598-633` (`drain` → `entry.capture` resubmits inline), `:732`, `:848`.
3. **F-R3-17 — HWM public type narrower than the uint64 contract.** `bindings/go/contracts/sockets.go:16-35` (alias of impl types), `internal/native/connection_socket.go:21-35`, `internal/native/socket_options.go:97-110` (`SetSendHighWaterMark(value int)`, getters return `int`), `socket_core.go:139-154` (getter rejects > MaxInt with EOVERFLOW). Common HWM projection (bindings README HWM table) requires the full `uint64_t` range. Change the public setters/getters to `uint64` (this is a public signature change, accepted pre-release: D-109/D-111); update docs comments in code, samples and tests; the native bridge already uses 8-byte uint64. Test: set/get of a value above `math.MaxInt64` round-trips.

